# Hazard Pressure 8 of 10 — clinging is not dying.
# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below
#
# A unit shoved into a pit clings, holds its activation slot, and is only Voided at the end
# of the following round — unless somebody adjacent finishes it, which costs neither half of
# an activation. Each of the four pits has open tiles on several sides, so the second unit
# you bring is not wasted: it stands by the rim and takes the free kick.
# The HighGround at (1,4) is the trap: fall damage lands while the unit is already clinging,
# and any damage to a clinging unit Voids it outright. Being shoved off there into the pit
# below is not a rescue problem, it is instant.

id: hz-08-free-kick
number: 208
name: Free Kick
description: Four pits with room to stand around them. Dropping something in only half kills it — finishing it from the rim is free, and so is what they do to you.

spawn h = Husk
spawn g = Grappler
spawn s = Stalker

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ..h.h.B
  .O...OB
  ^.....B
  .......
  .H...g^
  AO...O.
  AA.s.h#
